# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A fog ball that scatters but does not absorb, under a white sky. It must be invisible: every pixel reads the sky.
# @rt-performance Fast
# fog-furnace.pbrt -- a non-absorbing fog sphere under a uniform sky, bounded the pbrt-v4 way with
# Material "interface" (the shape has no BSDF of its own; the ray passes straight through).
#
# A furnace: every path through the fog either scatters (albedo 1) or passes, so with enough bounces the
# sphere is invisible against the sky. Within the bounce budget the three backends must still agree, which
# they only do when a boundary crossing leaves the MIS state of the last real vertex alone and the
# multiply-scattered light is weighted exactly once. Measured (centre of frame, empty sky = 1.0, depth 40):
# CPU 1.01, recursive 1.00, wavefront 1.01 at an optical radius of 3.
#
# Original, not derived from any distributed scene, so it carries no licence constraints.

LookAt  0 0 -6    0 0 0    0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 20 ]

Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 128 ] "integer yresolution" [ 128 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

LightSource "infinite" "rgb L" [ 0.6 0.7 0.9 ]

MakeNamedMedium "fog" "string type" [ "homogeneous" ]
  "rgb sigma_a" [ 0 0 0 ] "rgb sigma_s" [ 1 1 1 ] "float g" [ 0.3 ]

AttributeBegin
  Material "interface"
  MediumInterface "fog" ""
  Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 1 ]
AttributeEnd
